module beadCountDetection

manifest PolyBeads_LysisBuffer
manifest PBS

// ============================================================
// Measuring Droplet Volume in Home-Made Microfluidic Devices
// Protocol Source: Drop-seq / home-made microfluidic device
// calibration procedure (Harvard / McCarroll Lab style).
// DOI / Reference: standard lab protocol (no primary paper DOI).
//
// Purpose: Determine droplet volume in a home-made droplet-
// microfluidic device using monodisperse polystyrene beads as
// a volumetric calibration standard (Poisson-statistics-based
// droplet occupancy method).
//
// Reagents:
//   PolyBeads_LysisBuffer : durable, monodisperse polystyrene
//     beads (~10 um, carboxylated, e.g. Bangs Labs PC06N-11355
//     or fluorescent FC06F-10163) washed and resuspended in
//     Drop-seq lysis buffer at 1000 beads/uL. Loaded in syringe
//     with magnetic mixer as per standard barcoded-bead protocol.
//   PBS : phosphate-buffered saline loaded in the syringe
//     intended for cells. Co-flowing beads with PBS gives an
//     estimated bead concentration of 500 beads/uL in the
//     combined droplet fluid.
//
// Key calculation (post-detection):
//   Droplet occupancy  = (total beads counted) / (droplets counted)
//   Droplet volume     = occupancy / 500 beads per uL
//                      = # uL per droplet
//
// Device/Method scope:
//   This protocol is encoded for a DMF-adjacent or electrode-
//   actuated droplet-generation device. The syringe pump flows
//   are abstracted as dispense operations; the microfluidic
//   chip junction (where beads + PBS co-flow and generate
//   droplets) is abstracted as the first mix step. The bead-
//   counting step (several hundred droplets imaged under
//   microscope, beads counted per droplet) is abstracted as the
//   beadCountDetection module.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE (3 basic blocks):
//   BB1  main          -- dispense beads + PBS, co-flow and
//                         generate droplets, detect bead count
//                         occupancy signal
//   BB2  validDrop     -- beadSignal > 0: valid droplet
//                         population generated; dispose
//   BB3  invalidDrop   -- beadSignal <= 0: no detectable beads
//                         in droplets (device failure or zero
//                         droplet generation); drain
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense polystyrene bead suspension.
//   Beads (10 um carboxylated polystyrene, e.g. Bangs Labs
//   PC06N-11355 / fluorescent FC06F-10163) resuspended in
//   Drop-seq lysis buffer at 1000 beads/uL. Loaded into a
//   syringe with a magnetic mixer and drawn into syringe pump.
//   1 unit represents the bead-loaded syringe volume committed
//   to the droplet-generation run.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beadSuspension  = dispense 1 units of PolyBeads_LysisBuffer

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense PBS (cell-channel syringe).
//   The syringe intended for cells is loaded with regular PBS.
//   When co-flowing with the bead suspension at equal volume
//   ratio, the bead concentration in the combined aqueous phase
//   is halved: 1000 / 2 = 500 beads/uL in the droplet fluid.
//   1 unit represents the PBS syringe volume committed to the
//   same run.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsFlow         = dispense 1 units of PBS

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Co-flow and droplet generation.
//   Connect all tubing to the appropriate channels in the
//   microfluidic device. Both syringe pumps are started:
//   the bead syringe and the PBS syringe co-flow into the
//   aqueous inlet; the oil phase (carrier) generates droplets
//   at the T-junction or flow-focus nozzle.
//
//   NOTE ON ABSTRACTION: `mix` here models the co-flow
//   merging of the two aqueous streams at the chip inlet
//   junction, not a DMF electrode-merging event. The result
//   is a homogeneous bead-containing aqueous phase at
//   500 beads/uL that is subsequently broken into droplets
//   by the oil phase at the nozzle. Duration of 30s models
//   the stabilisation period before droplet collection begins.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

combinedFluid   = mix beadSuspension with pbsFlow for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Bead-counting detection (droplet occupancy).
//   Several hundred droplets are imaged under microscopy
//   (fluorescence if fluorescent beads are used; brightfield
//   otherwise). The total number of beads inside all counted
//   droplets is divided by the number of droplets counted to
//   yield the droplet occupancy (mean beads per droplet).
//
//   beadCountDetection module abstracts:
//     (a) image acquisition across >= several hundred droplets,
//     (b) bead segmentation and per-droplet counting,
//     (c) occupancy calculation: occupancy = total_beads /
//         total_droplets counted,
//     (d) volume calculation: droplet volume (uL) =
//         occupancy / 500 beads/uL.
//
//   Detection duration: 60s models the image acquisition
//   and automated counting window for a statistically
//   sound estimate (>= 200 droplets recommended).
//
//   beadSignal > 0 : beads detected in droplets; valid
//                    droplet population; occupancy and
//                    volume calculated successfully.
//   beadSignal <= 0 : no beads detected (device failure,
//                     clogged nozzle, or empty syringe);
//                     drain and troubleshoot.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

beadSignal      = detect beadCountDetection on combinedFluid for 60s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Droplet generation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): beadSignal > 0 -> beads detected in droplets;
//             valid droplet population and volume estimate
//             obtained; dispose combined fluid.
// Fail (BB3): beadSignal <= 0 -> no bead signal detected;
//             drain combined fluid (device failure path:
//             check tubing connections, nozzle, oil flow
//             rate, and bead resuspension quality).
// Both branches terminate after their respective operation.
// ============================================================

if (beadSignal > 0) {
    dispose combinedFluid
} else {
    drain combinedFluid
}

// ============================================================
// finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the bead detection QC signal. Experiment ends.
// Calculated droplet volume is available from the
// beadCountDetection module output log.
// ============================================================

dispose beadSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
